    "title": "Man wanted for attempted murder arrested by Morgan County Sheriff's Office - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Logan Sparkman ,\n6 hours ago\nMORGAN COUNTY, Ala. (WHNT) — Jail records show the Morgan County Sheriff’s Office found and arrested a man wanted for attempted murder it was searching for on Wednesday evening.\nMCSO said at 4:51 p.m. it was looking for Colton Ford Bone, 29, of Somerville. Bone was wanted for attempted murder, and officials said he should be considered armed and dangerous.\nJail records show Bone was arrested on the warrant for attempted murder and booked into the Morgan County Jail at 9:20 p.m. Wednesday.\nHis bond is set at $150,000 and he is still being held.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.\n17",
